Week 3 Report

Automation & Web Servers

DevOps Internship | Davine Technologies

1. Shell Scripting
    A shell script is a text file of commands executed by a shell such as Bash. Scripts automate repetitive
tasks (backups, user creation, log cleanup, deployments), reduce manual errors and make work
repeatable. Every script starts with a shebang (#!/bin/bash) and must be made executable with chmod
+x.
#!/bin/bash
echo "Hello, DevOps"
chmod +x hello.sh
./hello.sh

2. Variables
    Variables store values for reuse. They are assigned without spaces (NAME="value") and read with
$NAME. Scripts receive input through arguments ($1, $2) or the read command, and $(command)
captures a command's output.
NAME="DevOps"
read -p "Enter folder: " DIR
TODAY=$(date +%F)
echo "Hello $NAME, today is $TODAY"
SRC="${1:-/home/user/data}" # default value

3. Conditional Statements and Loops
    if/else and case statements let a script make decisions, such as checking that a directory exists before
backing it up. for and while loops repeat actions, for example creating several users or processing every
log file.
if [ -d "$SRC" ]; then
 echo "Found"
else
 echo "Missing"; exit 1
fi
for USER in user1 user2 user3; do
 echo "Creating $USER"
done

4. Functions
    Functions group reusable logic under a name, keeping scripts short and readable. A common example is a
logging function used throughout a script.
log() { echo "[$(date '+%F %T')] $1" | tee -a backup.log; }
log "Backup started"

5. Automation Scripts Created
    Script Purpose
sysinfo.sh Displays hostname, OS, kernel, uptime, IP, CPU, memory and disk usage
backup.sh Creates a timestamped .tar.gz backup of a directory
create_users_dirs.sh Creates users and personal directories with correct ownership and
permissions
clean_logs.sh Deletes .log files older than a set number of days using find -mtime
project_backup.sh Activity script: creates directories, copies files, backs up, compresses and
logs

6. Cron Jobs
    Cron is the Linux job scheduler. Jobs are defined in a crontab with five time fields (minute, hour, day of
month, month, day of week) followed by the command. Use absolute paths and redirect output to a log file
so failures can be investigated.
crontab -e
0 2 * * * /home/user/scripts/project_backup.sh >> /home/user/DevOps/Logs/cron.log 2>&1
crontab -l
Schedule Meaning
*/5 * * * * Every 5 minutes
0 2 * * * Every day at 2:00 AM
0 3 * * 0 Every Sunday at 3:00 AM

7. Apache Web Server
    Apache HTTP Server is a widely used, modular web server. Its default web root is /var/www/html and it
is managed with systemctl. Per-directory overrides are possible through .htaccess files.
sudo apt install -y apache2
sudo systemctl enable --now apache2
sudo cp index.html /var/www/html/
curl -I http://localhost

8. Nginx Web Server
    Nginx is an event-driven web server known for speed and low memory use. It is commonly used for static
content, as a reverse proxy and as a load balancer. Configuration is checked with nginx -t before
reloading.
Apache Nginx
Architecture Process/thread per connection Event-driven, asynchronous
Static content Good Excellent
Config Supports .htaccess Central config files only
Best for Flexible, module-rich setups High traffic, proxy, load balancing

9. Basic Web Server Configuration and Log Management
    Web servers write an access log (every request) and an error log (problems). Reviewing them is the first
step in troubleshooting. Old logs should be cleaned or rotated to save disk space, which is automated with
clean_logs.sh or logrotate.
sudo tail -f /var/log/apache2/access.log
sudo tail -n 50 /var/log/apache2/error.log
sudo tail -f /var/log/nginx/access.log

10. Hands-on Activity Summary
    Wrote a Bash script that creates project directories, copies files, generates a timestamped backup and
compresses it into an archive. Scheduled it with Cron to run daily at 2:00 AM, installed Apache, deployed a
simple HTML company website to /var/www/html and verified it in the browser and with curl.

11. Conclusion
    Week 3 showed how scripting and scheduling remove manual work, and how a web server publishes
content. These skills lead directly into containers, CI/CD pipelines and configuration management in later
weeks.